        "notes": "A bare rock with no atmosphere to carry heat, fitted to the light curve: 575 ± 10 K where the star is overhead, the limit for a perfectly dark surface, cooling toward the terminator and cold at night. It fits the ten visits as well as a free smooth map, whose hot spot also sits under the star. The data measure the day-to-night pattern; the shape across the disc comes from the rock model."
